<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Koga kubo</h1><p class="st-meta">1455 CE – 1583 CE (approx.) · capital Koga</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A branch of the Ashikaga that ruled from Koga in the Kanto for over a century, fighting the Uesugi and later becoming clients of the Later Hojo.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-shigeuji">Ashikaga Shigeuji</a>, the restored <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kamakura-fu">Kamakura kubo</a>, killed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto</a> deputy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-noritada">Uesugi Noritada</a> in 1454, starting the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyotoku-war">Kyotoku War</a>. In 1455 he lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> and moved his base to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koga-ibaraki">Koga</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimosa-province">Shimousa</a> province, from which his line took its name. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> sent a rival, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-masatomo">Ashikaga Masatomo</a>, who became the Horigoe kubo.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koga-ibaraki">Koga</a> kubo claimed authority over the eastern provinces and relied on alliances with local warrior families of the northern and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto</a>. Shigeuji fought the Uesugi for nearly thirty years. Later kubo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-masauji">Masauji</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-takamoto">Takamoto</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-haruuji">Haruuji</a>, were drawn into family feuds and the rise of the Later Hojo, who married into the line and controlled it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last kubo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshiuji">Ashikaga Yoshiuji</a>, was a Hojo puppet; on his death in 1583 the line ended. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> later gave his daughter's family a small estate as the Kitsuregawa.</p></div><aside class="st-